#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""release: release a version from its entry in docs/releases.md (dev/release.md, To release).

  scripts/release prepare VERSION   turn Unreleased into the entry of VERSION, dated today
                                    (Swedish time), and bump the version to it, for a pull
                                    request
  scripts/release tag VERSION       tag origin/main's head as vVERSION and push the tag, which
                                    starts .github/workflows/release.yml
  scripts/release notes VERSION     print the body of VERSION's GitHub release
  scripts/release check-tag VERSION check that the tag vVERSION can be released (release.yml)
  scripts/release lint              the version check of scripts/ci, with the release notes
  scripts/release check-pr BASE HEAD LABELS
                                    fail when the pull request from BASE to HEAD changes what a
                                    user sees but not Unreleased, unless LABELS (a JSON list of
                                    names) has "no release note" (ci.yml)

VERSION is spelled as frontend/package.json spells it (1.0.0-beta.2). prepare refuses a new
version while Unreleased says "Nothing yet.". It bumps backend/pyproject.toml (Python's spelling)
and frontend/package.json, refreshes the lock files (uv lock in backend/ and demo/, npm install
--package-lock-only in frontend/), renames Unreleased to the version with its metadata line and
puts a new Unreleased above it. When VERSION is the current version and has no tag yet, it keeps
the version and its entry: the bullets of Unreleased join the entry and its metadata line gets
today's date. Then it runs the lint and prints what to commit.

tag fetches origin and refuses unless origin/main's version is VERSION, its entry is dated the
date (Swedish time) of origin/main's head and the tag does not exist yet. notes prints the entry
without its heading and metadata line, with every relative link made absolute on the docs site
(https://tnek213.github.io/bwtidy/).
"""

import sys

from devlib import release

if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(release.main(sys.argv[1:], __doc__ or ""))
